{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"Implementation complete in worktree ../despotic-s1 (branch despotic-s1);\npushed as Gerrit change 1672 (commit 98ef247339, rebar-ticket trailer 248f-ac00-18db-4259).\n\n## What landed\n\n- NEW `peer_confirmations.py` (187 LOC): `PeerConfirmationStore` +\n  `record_key(source, target, relation)` + `open_store(repo_root)`, SCHEMA_VERSION 1, atomic\n  mkstemp/os.replace save, fail-OPEN load (corrupt or absent -> empty, never raises).\n- `dispatch_one.py`: `update_one` and `_update_one_dispatch_links` gain an optional\n  `link_confirm` keyword; `set_relationship`'s return value (previously discarded) is captured\n  so `result[\"id\"]` can be recorded as the vendor link id.\n- `dispatch_apply_phases.py`: `_confirm_link_add` — the swallow-everything invocation wrapper.\n- `apply_handlers.py`: `_make_link_confirm` builds the sink from `BatchApplyContext`\n  (`binding_store`, `pass_id`, `repo_root`) and `handle_update` passes it into `update_one`.\n- `git_adapter.py`: `PEER_CONFIRMATIONS_FILE` + `__all__` export.\n- `reconcile_helpers.py`: staged in BOTH `_rel_files` AND `_tracked_basenames`.\n\n## Three plan corrections the plan-review gate caught (all verified against the code first)\n\n1. Staging in `_rel_files` alone is INSUFFICIENT: `_commit_binding_store_snapshot` keeps a\n   second parallel `_tracked_basenames` set (the bug-1e08 per-file idempotency guard) and\n   returns \"already up-to-date\" when no tracked basename is staged, silently dropping a\n   confirmation-only change on every pass.\n2. The original plan's \"no key translation is needed\" was WRONG — the outbound ADD entry carries\n   Jira keys (`to_key`), not local ids, so the target needs `get_local_id` reverse-mapping and\n   an unbound target must record nothing rather than persist a vendor key in a local-id field.\n3. The write site was targeted at `apply_outbound._apply_outbound_update`, which is NOT the\n   production outbound-update path — production dispatches through `apply_handlers.handle_update`,\n   so the callback would never have fired in production. Rebuilt there instead, where\n   `BatchApplyContext` already carries everything needed (no new plumbing).\n\n## Module-size note\n\nAdding the helper inline pushed `dispatch_one.py` to 805 lines, OVER the 800 hard cap. Resolved\nby moving `_confirm_link_add` to the established sibling leaf `dispatch_apply_phases.py` (the\nsame seam ticket 744a/a3fa used for exactly this reason). Final sizes: dispatch_one 786,\ndispatch_apply_phases 416, apply_handlers 460, peer_confirmations 187, reconcile_helpers 675,\ngit_adapter 302 — all under 800.\n\n## Verification (worktree venv)\n\n- `pytest tests/unit/rebar_reconciler/apply/test_peer_confirmations_store.py` -> 20 passed\n- `pytest tests/unit/rebar_reconciler` -> 2421 passed (no regression)\n- `make lint` -> exit 0; `make typecheck` -> Success, 510 source files\n- MUTATION CHECK: removing `os.path.basename(git_adapter.PEER_CONFIRMATIONS_FILE)` from\n  `_tracked_basenames` turns `test_commit_only_peer_confirmations_is_staged_and_committed` RED\n  (\"confirmation-only change was not committed\"); restoring it turns it GREEN. The test pins the\n  bug-1e08 trap itself, not the diff.\n\nAwaiting LLM-Review +1 and Verified +1 before close."},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1786562143954410001,"uuid":"8c45932c-de64-4d75-af5b-6e3963d66c19"}